{
  "comment": [
    "Every class in tui.crossterm, registered for JNI.",
    "The crossterm native library constructs whichever event class the terminal produced and looks it up with JNI FindClass.",
    "native-image only keeps classes something references, so any event kind the Scala code does not mention by name is stripped",
    "and the lookup fails at runtime with NoClassDefFoundError - crashing the TUI the first time someone produces that event.",
    "Horizontal scroll (MouseEventKind$ScrollLeft) did exactly that. Registering the package removes the whole class of bug",
    "rather than the one that was reported. CrosstermJniMetadataTest keeps this list in step with the jar."
  ],
